                "2.4 Explanation\n",
                "\n",
                "The confusion matrix shows that the model predicts only the positive class (step = 1). While it correctly identifies many true step events, it incorrectly classifies all non-step events as steps. This indicates strong class bias toward predicting steps and suggests the model lacks the ability to detect negative cases."
              ]
